Z||000011||hugh||11-03-2000||10:02 PM||||Cooter,I didn't know it when I was young,but we were poor.I don't remember having crayons,but that may be because I am getting old and memory is the second thing to go.When someone had a television you could tell because of the crowd in front of their house watching it through their front windows.It was black and white and fascinating to see people in other parts of the country doing something and we could see it as it was done,but who could expect that someday we would have what we have now.I watched a fuzzy picture of an atomic blast somewhere out west in the late 40's and a clear picture of a man setting foot on the moon in 1969.Sorry for the long post,but I seem to have things come back to me when I talk about the past.Things I haven't thought of for many years.||||reg||1
